## Summary

Audited the codebase for structural simplifications and consolidated parallel task execution across calendar import, search loading, search planning and image-library search.

Before: calendar and search owned separate fan-out helpers, and image search repeated its own goroutine loop; each kept task values and errors in separate slices.
Now: `internal/parallel.Run` returns ordered `Result[T]` records pairing each value with its error. All former callers use it, and the old helpers and image-search loop are removed.

Before: search planning launched a goroutine per object and used a global semaphore to cap active bucket requests.
Now: its existing 16-task limit is enforced by the shared worker pool, and the semaphore is deleted.

Preserved ordering, concurrency ceilings, error messages, partial-success behavior and PDF voting. Kept the geocoder's in-place lookup pool and store lifecycle queues separate because their contracts differ. No schema, production-data or visible UI changes. Affected database tests, full import and image-search tests, helper concurrency tests with the race detector, repository-wide vet and diff checks passed. The requested merge from main reported already up to date; no conflict resolutions were needed.

